 {
  "key": "U06199",
  "en": "Hideyoshi's offensive was cunning.\nFirst he won Ukita Naoie over to the\nOda, then struck down the rebels\nAraki Murashige of Arioka Castle and\nBessho Nagaharu of Miki Castle.\n\nIshiyama Hongan-ji now made peace\nwith Nobunaga and withdrew to Kishu.\nAs Nobunaga's power grew, the Mouri\nwere forced wholly onto the\ndefensive.\n\nWithout pause, Hideyoshi moved on\nTajima, Inaba and Hoki, and besieged\nthe Mouri branch castle of Tottori.\nIn response, the Mouri sent Tsuneie,\nheir of Tsuneyasu of a Kikkawa\nbranch house, into Tottori Castle.\nTsuneie began siege preparations as\nsoon as he entered the castle, but\nhe could not gather enough\nprovisions, and time was wasted.\n\n\nEight years after Yamanaka\nShikanosuke's death, Hideyoshi's\nChugoku campaign was advancing\nsteadily under a meticulous plan..."
 },
